<title>JAPAN: Shares of Japan chip-making machine firms fall.</title>
<headline>Shares of Japan chip-making machine firms fall.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of semiconductor-producing equipment makers fell on late Tuesday afternoon in active trade on the Tokyo Stock Exchange due to profit-taking, traders said.</p>
<p>By 0543 GMT, shares of Tokyo Electron Ltd were down 310 yen at 7,340 in a turnover of 2.27 million shares.  </p>
<p>Canon Inc was down 100 yen at 3,590 with turnover of 1.69 million by 0543 GMT. By 0549 GMT, Advantest Corp had fallen 500 yen to 11,800 yen.</p>
<p>-Tokyo Equities desk [813] 3432-9404</p>
</text>
